#{[{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186144091 :tutorial/content "To multiply fractions, we multiply the numerators, multiply the denominators, and simplify (if necessary).\n\nFor example, to multiply $\\dfrac 1 {2} \\times \\dfrac 1 {3},$ we multiply the numerators and we multiply the denominators:\n\n$$\n\\dfrac{\\color{blue}1}{\\color{red}2} \\times \\dfrac{\\color{blue}1}{\\color{red}3} =  \\dfrac {{\\color{blue}1}\\times {\\color{blue}1}} {{\\color{red}2}\\times {\\color{red}3}} = \\dfrac{1}{6}\n$$\n\nNotice that we get the same answer when we use a fraction model.\n\n![](images/6d/6d4a0a382c9624510581d94e5829b2be6907e493aaba20eb471901f061b87820.png)" :tutorial/id #uuid "a71c2faa-d009-5288-8863-51238a73c406" :tutorial/math-academy-id 8927 :tutorial/title "Introduction"}]}
